            <ArticleTitle>[The anisotropy of the skin of the precordial area in patients with stable and unstable stenocardia].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>20-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary patients were studied for the precordial area skin anisotropic properties with the aid of EHF differential-diagnostic reflectometry. Disclosed in the patients were the following points of anisotropia: E18S in the 5th intercostal space along the medioclavicular line on the left, E18D--a symmetric point on the right, R24S in the 3d intercostal space along the parasternal line on the left, R24D--a symmetric point on the right. The value for anisotropia determined by anisotropia factor in decibels will rest with the degree of abnormal changes on the cardiac muscle, which fact has been documented by electrocardiographic findings.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
